      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus and the chain rule, f'(x)=x^4\\cos x-(-x^3)^4\\cos(-x^3)(-3x^2)=x^4\\cos x+3x^{14}\\cos(x^3). Hence f'(1)=4\\cos 1, option e. No captured Math Academy answer or grade confirms its key.",
