      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "In Gram–Schmidt applied in the listed order, the third basis vector (a,b,c) is orthogonal to the first vector (2,0,2). Therefore 2a+2c=0, giving a/c=-1. Explicitly, the third vector is (-3/2,6,3/2), so c is nonzero. This selects option d. No captured Math Academy answer or grade confirms its key.",
