        "reasoning": "Integrating first with respect to y gives \\int_0^1 \\frac{x^2}{2}[(2-x)^2-(x-1)^2]\\,dx=\\int_0^1(\\frac{3}{2}x^2-x^3)\\,dx=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}, option e. No captured Math Academy answer or grade confirms its key.",
