      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "Set y=tu(t). Substitution gives t^3u''+4t^2u'=0, so u'=Ct^{-4} and u=D+Et^{-3}. Thus a second independent solution is y₂=t^{-2}, and the general solution is y=At+B/t², option d. No captured Math Academy answer or grade confirms its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "y=At+\\frac{B}{{t}^{2}}",
