      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "The transformed equation is (s+3)Y=1+(s+2)/(s²+4), giving Y=(s²+s+6)/[(s+3)(s²+4)]. Its partial fractions are 12/[13(s+3)]+(s+10)/[13(s²+4)]. Inverting gives y(t)=(12/13)e^{-3t}+(5/13)sin(2t)+(1/13)cos(2t), which satisfies the equation and y(0)=1. No captured Math Academy answer or grade confirms its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
