        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "Set v=y′, so y′=v and v′=(y−4v)/x². Two Euler steps use h=1/2 and update both variables from the previous point. From (x,y,v)=(1,−1,2), the first step gives y=0 and v=−5/2 at x=3/2. The second gives y(2)=0+(1/2)(−5/2)=−5/4 and v(2)=−5/2+(1/2)[10/(9/4)]=−5/18. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
