        "reasoning": "Completing the squares gives (x−3)²+4y²−(z+1)²=0, or (z+1)²=(x−3)²+4y². This is an elliptic cone with vertex and center of symmetry (3,0,−1), so option c is mathematically correct. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
