      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "Write x=a(5,−3)+b(−7,6). Then 5a−7b=18 and −3a+6b=−9. Doubling the first equation and adding seven times the second gives −11a=−27? Instead, doubling the second and adding three times the first gives 9a−9b=36, so a−b=4. Substitution gives b=1 and a=5. Thus [x]_B=(5,1), option e. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]",
            "correct_option": "e",
            "value_type": "math",
            "wrong_value": "[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]",
            "correct_keys": [],
