      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "For an orthonormal basis, the coordinates are the dot products with the basis vectors. They are [2(−3)−5]/√5=−11/√5 and [−3+2(5)]/√5=7/√5, giving option a. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]",
