      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "For λ>0, y=A cos(3λx)+B sin(3λx). The condition y(0)=0 forces A=0, and a nonzero solution satisfies sin(3λπ)=0. Thus λ_n=n/3 for n=1,2,…, with eigenfunctions B_n sin(3λ_n x)=B_n sin(nx), where B_n≠0. At λ=0, the boundary conditions permit only the zero solution. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
