        "reasoning": "Y(s)=e^{-2s}/[s(s+1)(s+2)], and 1/[s(s+1)(s+2)]=1/(2s)−1/(s+1)+1/[2(s+2)]. Inverting and applying the time shift gives y(t)=u(t−2)[1/2−e^{−(t−2)}+(1/2)e^{−2(t−2)}]. Thus the blank is (1/2)e^{−2(t−2)}. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "correct_value": "\\frac{1}{2}e^{-2(t-2)}",
            "correct_option": null,
            "value_type": "math",
            "wrong_value": "-\\frac{1}{2}e^{-2(t-2)}",
            "correct_keys": [],
            "wrong_keys": [],
            "ma_value": null,
            "ma_basis": "none",
