      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "The symmetric matrix of Q is A=[[-2,2,0],[2,1,0],[0,0,-1]]. A maximizing unit vector satisfies Ax=2x, giving x₂=2x₁ and x₃=0. Normalization yields x=(1,2,0)/√5, option d, and substitution gives Q(x)=2. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "correct_value": "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]",
            "correct_option": "d",
            "value_type": "math",
            "wrong_value": "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]",
            "correct_keys": [],
            "wrong_keys": [],
