      "solution": {
        "status": "unavailable",
        "reasoning": "A potential function is φ(x,y)=x³y³+x²−2y², whose gradient equals F. The curve runs from (0,1) to (1,e), so the integral is φ(1,e)−φ(0,1)=e³+1−2e²−(−2)=e³−2e²+3, option c. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
